codex
Implemented a deterministic, native Track A generator for the square of a Hamilton cycle, based on Theorem 1.7 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.14794).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2502_14794.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/gen_2502_14794.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2502.14794/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes all gates:

- G4: 0/200,000 valid structure-aware guesses.
- G5/G6: six attacks failed on 8/8 seeds; exact DFS exhausted 2,000,008 nodes.
- G8: 60/60 relabelling and witness-transport checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct.
- G9(c): 374 characters, 96 elements, 288 intended operations.
- G1 was rechecked on all 16 preset/seed combinations after the final edits.

The only unresolved requirement is external oracle evidence. The repository hardener was run, but all requests received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “total key limit” before any valid attempt. The transcript records these honestly; it does not constitute a hardness verdict. The paper is therefore neither rejected nor fully release-ready until quota is restored and the bare, structural-hint, and placebo runs are repeated.
