../../results/2411.04916/README.md:11:The paper itself proves geometric lower bounds, not a complexity theorem. The scalable hardness statement comes from Cavallaro and Fluschnik, [Section 3.2, Theorem 2](https://arxiv.org/html/2104.08470#S3.SS2): 3-colouring remains NP-hard even for 5-regular planar Hamiltonian graphs. Our hidden core is likewise 5-regular, the number of vertices grows, and the witness space is `3^n`; there is no optimum or nonexistence claim.
